[32m+[m[32m- `NAK(e)` also acknowledges `e − 1`: the receiver NAKs only its next expected sequence, so everything before `e` has been delivered.[m
[32m+[m[32m- An `ACK` arriving while a replay is in progress moves the replay pointer forward past acknowledged flits; the replay is not restarted.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The `MAX_RETRY` escalation fires once per stuck sequence (on the `(MAX_RETRY+1)`-th NAK of the same `e`); the counter is cleared when `e` is acknowledged.[m
[32m+[m[32m- NAK density uses consecutive (tumbling) windows of `nak_window_flits` received flits and fires at most once per window; NAKs counted include re-sends.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Timer defaults (assumed parameters, `configs/default.yaml`): ACK every 8 deliveries or after 16 cycles without one; NAK re-send after `2 × (channel + sideband latency) + 32` = 64 link cycles; replay timeout `4 ×` that = 256 cycles. The re-send interval must exceed the NAK → replay round trip (21 link cycles measured at the default latencies, m2_report.md), otherwise one error would cause several replays.[m
